cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Multi-objective evolutionary feature selection on high-dimensional
  biological data, with a knockoff baseline
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it."
type: software
abstract: >-
  A budget-matched comparison of NSGA-II feature selection against random
  subsets, standard filter and embedded baselines, a model-X knockoff filter,
  and an oracle with access to the true support. Evaluated under nested
  cross-validation with a labels-permuted control, and reported with Friedman
  ranks, Holm-corrected pairwise Wilcoxon tests, Cliff's delta effect sizes,
  and hypervolume against a fixed, problem-derived reference point.
keywords:
  - feature selection
  - multi-objective optimisation
  - NSGA-II
  - knockoff filter
  - false discovery rate
  - nested cross-validation
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-14"
